-          <p>The Products may allow a limited number of successful export actions at no charge. The current consumer offer is 5 free exports. A successful manual, scheduled, Shortcut, or direct action may count against the same allowance as shown in the Product, regardless of how many dates or files it contains. Failed work and retries can be treated differently under the documented quota rules.</p>
-          <p>Where offered, Full Access is a one-time in-app purchase that removes the export limit for supported features. It is not a subscription and does not renew. Apple platforms may offer Individual Lifetime, Family Lifetime, or an upgrade between them; other stores can offer their own supported one-time product. The store purchase sheet controls the displayed product, price, currency, tax, account, and Family Sharing eligibility.</p>
-          <p>A “lifetime” or permanent entitlement means the purchased license does not expire on a recurring billing schedule. It does not guarantee that every feature, operating system, device, provider, or Product will remain available or supported forever. We may change future pricing or offers without changing a completed purchase except as allowed by the store terms and law.</p>
-          <p>Purchases, restores, billing, and refunds are handled by the store where you bought Full Access. We do not receive full card details and ordinarily cannot issue a store refund directly. For Apple purchases, use <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Report a Problem</a>; for Google Play purchases, use Google's applicable refund flow. Refund eligibility is determined by the store and applicable law.</p>
+          <h2>10. Paid access, subscriptions, and refunds</h2>
+          <p>On the subscription-enabled iPhone, iPad, and Google Play phone releases, setup and exports require an active store-backed trial, subscription, Lifetime purchase, or preserved permanent entitlement. There is no local free-export allowance. The Mac companion and F-Droid included-access channel remain free. Older distributed versions can have different offers.</p>
+          <p>Individual access is available through weekly or yearly auto-renewable subscriptions or a one-time Lifetime purchase. Apple platforms also offer Family Sharing products and an upgrade for eligible Individual Lifetime or legacy owners. Google Play products are Individual-only; purchases do not transfer between stores. Family Sharing shares feature access, not health records or exported files.</p>
+          <p>Eligible subscriptions include a 7-day free trial, then renew automatically at the price and billing interval shown by the store before confirmation. The store determines introductory eligibility. Lifetime is charged immediately once, has no trial, and does not renew. The purchase sheet controls the product, local price, currency, tax and applicable terms.</p>
+          <p>Manage or cancel through the purchasing Apple or Google account. For Apple subscriptions, cancel at least 24 hours before the trial or current period ends; follow any cancellation deadline shown for your store offer. Deleting the app or buying Lifetime does not cancel an existing subscription. When access expires or is revoked, new exports and setup are gated; previously exported files remain yours.</p>
+          <p>Existing paid and previously grandfathered access remains valid. Restore Purchases restores eligible access, not deleted health data or files. A subscription alone does not qualify for the discounted Family Lifetime upgrade. A permanent entitlement has no recurring expiration, but does not guarantee indefinite device, provider or feature support.</p>
+          <p>Apple or Google handles billing, purchase restoration and refunds under its terms and applicable law. We do not receive full payment-card details. Use Apple's <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com/">Report a Problem</a> or Google's applicable refund process. These terms do not limit mandatory consumer rights or announce a future price increase.</p>
